# Fog settings

option.BORDER_FOG                           = Border Fog
option.BORDER_FOG.comment                   = Thick fog that extends to the edges of the render distance. Helps hide chunk borders and creates a more seamless transition to the void.
option.CAVE_FOG                             = Cave Fog
option.CAVE_FOG.comment                     = Light, slightly glowing fog applied underground. Enhances cavern atmosphere and helps illuminate cave interiors without significantly impacting performance.
option.BLOOMY_FOG                           = Bloomy Fog
option.BLOOMY_FOG.comment                   = Intense bloom effect within fog. Simulates light from bright objects scattering within fog volumes. Illuminates areas behind bright objects. Minimal performance impact.
option.BLOOMY_FOG_INTENSITY                 = Bloomy Fog Intensity
option.BLOOMY_FOG_INTENSITY.comment         = Adjusts the intensity of "bloomy fog"
option.OVERWORLD_FOG_INTENSITY              = Overworld Fog Intensity
option.OVERWORLD_FOG_INTENSITY.comment    = Controls the intensity of overworld fog. Higher values create denser fog near the ground, lower values make fog thinner.

value.MIST_MODE.MIST_MODE_OFF              = Off
value.MIST_MODE.MIST_MODE_BASIC            = Basic
value.MIST_MODE.MIST_MODE_ADVANCED         = Advanced
option.MIST_MODE                           = Ground Mist
option.MIST_MODE.comment                  = Ground-hugging haze layer. Off = disabled. Basic = two-octave noise mist with density-varying phase and wetness coupling. Advanced = adds per-step sun self-shadowing with cloud occlusion and grazing-angle cost gating.
option.MIST_MODE_OFF                       = Off
option.MIST_MODE_BASIC                     = Basic
option.MIST_MODE_ADVANCED                  = Advanced
option.MIST_DENSITY                        = Mist Density
option.MIST_DENSITY.comment               = Overall thickness of the mist layer. Higher values produce denser, more opaque ground fog.
option.MIST_ALTITUDE                       = Mist Ceiling
option.MIST_ALTITUDE.comment              = Maximum altitude (blocks) above which mist cannot exist. Lower values keep mist close to the ground.
option.MIST_FALLOFF_RATE                   = Mist Falloff Rate
option.MIST_FALLOFF_RATE.comment          = How quickly mist thins with altitude above sea level. Higher = thinner layer, lower = mist reaches higher.
option.MIST_SEA_LEVEL_BIAS                 = Mist Sea Level Bias
option.MIST_SEA_LEVEL_BIAS.comment        = Shifts the mist base up or down relative to the configured sea level. Positive = mist starts higher, negative = mist starts lower.
option.MIST_SHADOW_STEPS                   = Mist Shadow Steps
option.MIST_SHADOW_STEPS.comment          = Number of ray-march steps toward the sun for mist self-shadowing (Advanced mode only). Higher = more accurate self-shadowing at higher GPU cost.
option.VL                                   = Volumetric Fog
option.LPV_VL.comment                       = Light sources illuminate the fog volume. Requires Colored Lights enabled. Adds realistic light propagation through fog. Significant performance impact. 
option.VL.comment                           = Adds volumetric fog with light shafts and variable density. Creates atmosphere and sun rays streaming through the fog. Requires significant GPU resources.
option.VL_RENDER_SCALE                      = VL Render Scale
option.VL_RENDER_SCALE.comment = Controls vl render scale.
option.AIR_FOG_CLOUDY_NOISE                 = Cloudy Fog
option.AIR_FOG_CLOUDY_NOISE.comment         = Subtle cloud-like shapes within the fog, best visible in morning light. Requires volumetric fog to be enabled for the effect to appear.
option.AIR_FOG_COLORED_LIGHT_SHAFTS         = Colored Light Shafts
option.AIR_FOG_COLORED_LIGHT_SHAFTS.comment    = Light shafts passing through translucent objects are tinted by their color. Creates colorful god rays effect when sunlight passes through leaves and glass.
option.AIR_FOG_COLORED_LIGHT_SHAFTS_INTENSITY         = Colored Light Shafts Intensity
option.AIR_FOG_COLORED_LIGHT_SHAFTS_INTENSITY.comment = Controls the strength of the color tinting applied to light shafts

