option.COLOR_GRADING                    = Color Grading
option.COLOR_GRADING.comment            = Enables the full color grading pipeline. When on: applies brightness/contrast/saturation, white balance, ASC CDL three-way lift/gamma/gain, perceptual Oklab contrast, selective hue/saturation per color range, shadow and highlight tints, and black/white point. When off: the tonemapper output is used as-is with no further grading.
option.ACADEMY_EXPOSURE                 = ACES Exposure
option.ACADEMY_EXPOSURE.comment         = Pre-tonemap exposure offset in stops fed into the ACES curve. +1 = twice as bright entering the curve, -1 = half as bright. Shifts where highlights roll off without changing the overall scene brightness.
option.ACADEMY_CONTRAST                = ACES Contrast
option.ACADEMY_CONTRAST.comment        = Steepness of the ACES S-curve. Above 1.0 deepens blacks and brightens highlights for a punchier look. Below 1.0 flattens the curve for a softer, lower-contrast output.
option.ACADEMY_SATURATION              = ACES Saturation
option.ACADEMY_SATURATION.comment      = Scales chroma inside the ACES operator before the final curve is applied. 1.0 = unchanged, 0.0 = greyscale. Interacts with highlight rolloff so saturated highlights compress naturally.
option.ACADEMY_HIGHLIGHT_ROLLOFF       = ACES Highlight Rolloff
option.ACADEMY_HIGHLIGHT_ROLLOFF.comment = How aggressively ACES compresses values above middle grey toward white. Higher = softer, more gradual rolloff with retained highlight detail. Lower = harder clipping, more contrasty sky and sun.
option.ACADEMY_SHADOW_TOE              = ACES Shadow Toe
option.ACADEMY_SHADOW_TOE.comment      = Lifts the bottom of the ACES curve, preventing pure black and adding a subtle shadow lift. Higher = more lifted blacks with visible shadow detail, filmic look.
option.ACADEMY_COLORFULNESS            = ACES Colorfulness
option.ACADEMY_COLORFULNESS.comment    = Shifts the ACES color appearance model toward more vivid (+) or more neutral (-) rendering. Positive values increase apparent chroma in midtones without affecting luminance.
option.AGX_EXPOSURE                    = AGX Exposure
option.AGX_EXPOSURE.comment            = Pre-tonemap exposure offset in stops fed into the AGX curve. +1 = twice as bright entering the curve. Shifts where highlights begin to compress.
option.AGX_CONTRAST                    = AGX Contrast
option.AGX_CONTRAST.comment            = Slope of the AGX S-curve. Above 1.0 = deeper blacks and brighter highlights. Below 1.0 = flatter, lower-contrast output. AGX handles saturated highlights more gracefully than ACES.
option.AGX_SATURATION                  = AGX Saturation
option.AGX_SATURATION.comment          = Scales chroma inside the AGX operator before the tonemap curve. 1.0 = unchanged. AGX's gamut compression means oversaturated colors roll off smoothly rather than clipping.
option.AGX_HIGHLIGHT_ROLLOFF           = AGX Highlight Rolloff
option.AGX_HIGHLIGHT_ROLLOFF.comment   = Controls how AGX compresses bright values toward white. Higher = softer rolloff with more retained highlight detail and color. Lower = harder, more contrasty highlights.
option.AGX_PUNCH                      = AGX Punch
option.AGX_PUNCH.comment               = Boosts midtone contrast and saturation for a punchier, more vivid look. Positive = more pop and color intensity in midtones. Negative = flatter, more muted and filmic output.
option.AGX_GOLDEN                     = AGX Golden
option.AGX_GOLDEN.comment              = Shifts the AGX output toward a warm golden tint. Positive = warmer, more cinematic golden grade. Negative = cooler, more neutral or bluish output.
